# Build context exclusions for kbbi-api.
#
# Without this, `node_modules` (hundreds of MB after a pnpm install), the 143MB
# dataset and the whole .git directory are sent as build context and, where the
# Dockerfile has a matching COPY, copied into the image. The build gets slow and
# the layer cache misses on every source edit.

# Dependencies: reinstalled inside the image from the lockfile. Copying the host
# tree would also carry absolute paths pnpm wrote for a different directory.
node_modules
.pnpm-store

# Git history: not needed to build, and it changes on every commit, which would
# invalidate the cache for the COPY steps above it.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Generated dictionary dump (74MB). Rebuilt inside the builder stage by
# `pnpm run prepare-data`, so shipping the host copy would both bloat the
# context and risk baking a dump generated from a different dataset.
kv-data

# The upstream dataset is fetched by CI, not committed. It must be present in
# the context for the builder's COPY, so it is deliberately NOT excluded here —
# see the fetch step in .github/workflows/ci.yml.

# Secrets and local noise
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log
.DS_Store

# Docs and editor state
*.md
!README.md
LICENSE
.claude
.hermes
.idea
.vscode
